      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "warn",
        "label": {
          "en": "⚠ Common Traps & Exam Pitfalls",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<strong>Inequality bounds for discrete distributions:</strong> Unlike continuous variables, strict inequalities make a critical difference:<br>&bull; \\(P(X \\ge r) = 1 - P(X \\le r - 1)\\) (NOT \\(1 - P(X \\le r)\\))<br>&bull; \\(P(X > r) = 1 - P(X \\le r)\\)<br>&bull; \\(P(X < r) = P(X \\le r - 1)\\).<br><br><strong>'At least one' complement shortcut:</strong> \\(P(X \\ge 1) = 1 - P(X = 0) = 1 - (1-p)^n\\). Always look for this time-saving identity in exam questions.<br><br><strong>Four binomial conditions:</strong> Cambridge exam questions frequently ask you to state assumptions justifying the binomial model: (1) Fixed number of trials \\(n\\), (2) Constant probability of success \\(p\\), (3) Independent trials, (4) Exactly two mutually exclusive outcomes (success/failure).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Exact probability",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>\\(X\\sim B(8,0.3)\\). Find (a) \\(P(X=3)\\), (b) \\(P(X\\leq1)\\).</p><p>(a) \\(P(X=3)=\\binom{8}{3}(0.3)^3(0.7)^5=56\\times0.027\\times0.16807\\approx0.2541\\).</p><p>(b) \\(P(X=0)=(0.7)^8\\approx0.0576\\); \\(P(X=1)=8(0.3)(0.7)^7\\approx0.1977\\). \\(P(X\\leq1)\\approx0.2553\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Finding n from mean",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>The mean of \\(X\\sim B(n,0.4)\\) is 6. Find \\(n\\) and the standard deviation.</p>\\[np=6\\Rightarrow n=15.\\quad\\sigma=\\sqrt{15\\times0.4\\times0.6}=\\sqrt{3.6}\\approx1.90.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example C — Algebraic Structure & Vieta's Root Relations",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Solve the quadratic equation \\( x^2 - 13x + 36 = 0 \\) and verify the sum and product of its roots.<br><br><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br><ol><li>Factor into binomials: \\( (x - 4)(x - 9) = 0 \\implies x = 4 \\text{ or } x = 9 \\).</li><li>Check Vieta's formulas: sum \\( = 4 + 9 = \\mathbf{13} \\) and product \\( = (4)(9) = \\mathbf{36} \\).</li></ol>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example D — Algebraic Structure & Vieta's Root Relations",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Solve the quadratic equation \\( x^2 - 10x + 25 = 0 \\) and verify the sum and product of its roots.<br><br><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br><ol><li>Factor into binomials: \\( (x - 5)(x - 5) = 0 \\implies x = 5 \\text{ or } x = 5 \\).</li><li>Check Vieta's formulas: sum \\( = 5 + 5 = \\mathbf{10} \\) and product \\( = (5)(5) = \\mathbf{25} \\).</li></ol>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "A fair coin is tossed 10 times. Find the probability of getting (a) exactly 6 heads, (b) fewer than 3 heads.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "(a) \\(\\binom{10}{6}(0.5)^{10}=210\\times\\tfrac{1}{1024}\\approx0.2051\\). (b) \\(P(X\\leq2)=P(0)+P(1)+P(2)=\\tfrac{1+10+45}{1024}=\\tfrac{56}{1024}\\approx0.0547\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "In a manufacturing batch, 5% of components are defective. A sample of 12 components is inspected. Find the probability that at least 2 components are defective.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Let \\(X \\sim B(12, 0.05)\\). We need \\(P(X \\ge 2) = 1 - [P(X = 0) + P(X = 1)]\\). \\(P(X = 0) = (0.95)^{12} \\approx 0.5404\\). \\(P(X = 1) = 12(0.05)(0.95)^{11} \\approx 0.3413\\). Thus, \\(P(X \\ge 2) = 1 - (0.5404 + 0.3413) = 1 - 0.8817 = 0.118\\) (3 s.f.).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
